.TH SUNFLOWER 1 "November 2026" "Sunflower 0.7" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sunflower \- twin-panel file manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sunflower
[\fIOPTION\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sunflower is a small and highly customizable twin-panel file manager with
support for plugins.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show help options.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Show version number.
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-no\-plugins\fR
Skip loading additional plugins.
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-no\-load\-tabs\fR
Skip loading additional tabs.
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-left\-tab\fR=\fIDIRECTORY\fR
Open new tab on the left notebook.
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-right\-tab\fR=\fIDIRECTORY\fR
Open new tab on the right notebook.
.TP
\fB\-L\fR, \fB\-\-left\-terminal\fR=\fIDIRECTORY\fR
Open terminal tab on the left notebook.
.TP
\fB\-R\fR, \fB\-\-right\-terminal\fR=\fIDIRECTORY\fR
Open terminal tab on the right notebook.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SUNFLOWER_GTK
Set to \fB4\fR to start the experimental GTK 4 interface.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/sunflower/
Configuration files.
.TP
.I ~/.config/sunflower/user_plugins/
Plugins installed by the user.
.SH AUTHOR
Sunflower was written by Mladen Mijatov and contributors.
